<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Consider an autonomous differential equation described by   
  <md>
    <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt} \amp= f(x),</mrow>
    <mrow>f(x) \amp=x^2 - 4x + c</mrow>
  </md>
  where <m>c</m> is a parameter. The function <m>f(x)</m> is graphed below. Use the slider to observe how the graph of <m>f</m> changes for different values of the parameter <m>c</m>.</p>

  <slider name="c" from="-10" to="10" showValue="false" initialValue="-4" step="1">
    <label><m>c = $c.value</m></label>
  </slider>
  <graph xmin="-5" ymin="-16" ymax="16" aspectRatio="1" grid="true">
    <function name="f">x^2 -4x + $c</function>
    <point name="equilibrium1" styleNumber="3">(2+sqrt(4 - $c),0)
    <label><m>E_1</m></label>
    </point>
    <point name="equilibrium2" styleNumber="3" hide="$c=4">(2-sqrt(4 - $c),0)
    <label><m>E_2</m></label>
    </point>
  </graph>
<p>The $equilibrium1.styleDescription triangles indicate equilibrium locations for the system, or values of <m>x</m> for which <m>\frac{dx}{dt} = 0</m>.</p>
<p>How many equilibria are present when <m>c = 0</m>?</p>
  <answer>2</answer>

<p>How many equilibria are present when <m>c = 5</m>?</p>
  <answer>0</answer>

<p>How many equilibria are present when <m>c = 4</m>?</p>
  <answer>1</answer>
<p>A bifurcation point occurs where the behavior of the system changes, i.e. in this case, where the number of equilibria changes. Which of the following is a bifurcation point for the given system?</p>
  <answer>
    <choice credit="1"><m>c = 4</m></choice>
    <choice><m>c = 0</m></choice>
    <choice><m>c = -4</m></choice>
    <choice><m>c = -10</m></choice>
  </answer>
  
</exercise>
</problem>
</section>




